    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d713">

                <pb facs="0671" n="659" xml:id="pg659"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.0090F/15: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-08T10:00:00+03:06">February 8,
                            1944—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:06 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>41. Plans for consular representation in Dhahran referred to in Department’s 17,
                    January 29, 3 p.m., discussed with Amir Faisal February 6.</p>
                <p>His personal reaction appeared favorable though he promised nothing more than a
                    reply after having referred matter to King.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
